[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605261216-igata-r1-benchtop-commissioning", :adr/title "igata R1 — Benchtop ≤500 ton HPDC commissioning and Council baseline", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# igata R1 — Benchtop ≤500 ton HPDC commissioning and Council baseline\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-26\n**Author:** Jun Kawasaki\n**Status:** Proposed\n\n## Context\n\nR0 (ADR-2605261200) established igata (鋳型) as religious-corp first-party HPDC / megacasting Tier-B actor with **14 constitutional gates G1..G14 + 10 non-goals N1..N10** IMMUTABLE R0..R3. The R0 scaffold landed 8 `igata_*` Pregel cells with import-time `RuntimeError` Council activation gates (silicon Wave 1 + yakushi Wave 1 pattern) and 5 lexicons under `com.etzhayyim.igata.*`.\n\nR1 transitions from R0 scaffold to **operational benchtop readiness** by establishing:\n\n1. **Council Lv6+ ≥3 attestation baseline** (`silenIgataReview` scope: `r1-benchtop-500ton-baseline`)\n2. **SME registration block**: HPDC engineer DID + metallurgist DID + 危険物取扱主任者-equivalent operator DID\n3. **Benchtop ≤500 ton HPDC PoC protocol** — small structural parts ≤200 g (bracket / hinge / sensor housing reference geometry), AlSi9Mg0.3 HT-free alloy baseline, single-cavity H13 die\n4. **7-cell activation** (`alloy_melt` + `die_preparation` + `shot_injection` + `solidification_eject` + `post_cast_qc` + `trim_machining` + `part_attestation` on naphtali + zebulun + joseph + levi + simeon); **`heat_treatment` stays R2-gated** (R1 = HT-free recipe only, T5 / T6 deferred to R2 ADR-2605261230)\n5. **Equipment procurement protocol** — second-hand revival preferred over new-build (vendor lock-in avoidance, §2(e) anti-gatekeeping pro-clearance value)\n6. **R1 exit / R2 entry criteria** — ≥30 consecutive successful shots / material balance ≥90% / multi-cavity die design Council-attested / vacuum-assist subsystem Council-attested / Hibachi PoC firmware tested\n7. **Confirms all 14 constitutional gates (G1..G14) + 10 non-goals (N1..N10) remain unchanged** — **no constitutional amendment**\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. Benchtop ≤500 ton HPDC PoC Protocol\n\n**Target:** AlSi9Mg0.3 single-piece reference part, 50–200 g final mass, as-cast yield ≥150 MPa, dimensional ±0.1 mm at die-finished surface, porosity ≤ ASTM E155 class 4.\n\n**R1 invariants (additive to G1..G14, not amendments):**\n\n- **HPDC clamping force**: ≤500 ton in R1 (G1 R0..R3 ceiling = ≤6000 ton; R1 R-phase sub-ceiling)\n- **Alloy recipe**: AlSi9Mg0.3 HT-free baseline only (5-element + Sr modifier per G7=NONE; T5 / T6 = R2)\n- **Die**: Single-cavity H13 hot-work tool steel; FreeCAD `.fcstd` source format mandatory (G3 vendor-free CAD)\n- **Vacuum-assist**: Optional in R1, recommended for ≤200 g thin-wall parts (R2 mandatory)\n- **Reference parts** (any 1 of 3 for first qualification shot):\n  - Bracket: 80 mm × 50 mm × 8 mm, ~60 g, single hole pattern\n  - Hinge: 100 mm × 40 mm × 5 mm, ~80 g, pivot axis hole\n  - Sensor housing: 60 mm × 60 mm × 30 mm, ~150 g, internal cavity for sensor PCB\n- **Shot sequence**: Slow phase 0.15 m/s × 800 ms → fast phase 3.2 m/s × 80 ms → intensification 100 MPa × 2 s\n- **All shot profiles @ 1 kHz logged** per G8 (position + velocity + pressure + die surface temp at 4 thermocouple positions)\n\n### 2. Council Lv6+ Attestation Baseline: `r1-benchtop-500ton-baseline`\n\n**Scope:** Single `silenIgataReview` NDJSON record with:\n- `reviewType: \"r1-benchtop-500ton-baseline\"` (from R0 lexicon `knownValues`)\n- `councilAttestationCount: ≥3` (Lv6+ supermajority per ADR-2605192300)\n- `approvedRPhase: \"R1\"`\n- `approvedClampingForceTons: 500`\n- `approvedAlloyRecipes: [\"AlSi9Mg0.3-HT-free\"]`\n- `approvedDieMaterials: [\"H13-hot-work-tool-steel\"]`\n- `approvedRoboticsClasses: [\"Otete-heat-resistant\", \"Mimi-dimensional-2D-radiograph\"]` (X-ray CT = R2; 2D radiograph OK for R1 screening)\n- `verdict: \"approved\"` (or `approved-with-conditions`)\n- `attestationUri: \"at://...did:plc:[council-multisig-actor]/com.etzhayyim.igata.silenIgataReview/...\"` (published via `council.etzhayyim.com` Bluesky PDS)\n\n**Gate unlock condition:** Both `COUNCIL_CHARTER_ATTESTATION_TX_HASH` (Base L2 Council Lv6+ multisig Tx hash) and `SILEN_IGATA_BASELINE_REVIEW_CID` (IPFS CID of the `silenIgataReview` record) set non-`None` in the 7 R1-activated `igata_*` cells (`alloy_melt` / `die_preparation` / `shot_injection` / `solidification_eject` / `post_cast_qc` / `trim_machining` / `part_attestation`).\n\n**`heat_treatment` cell stays R2-gated** — `R2_HT_RECIPE_BASELINE_CID` (T5 / T6 protocol attestation) additional gate not satisfied at R1.\n\n**Timing:** Council motion during 2026-06 meeting; execution by 2026-07-31.\n\n### 3. SME Registration Block\n\n**Three SME DIDs required for R1 activation** (parallel to yakushi Wave 1 `QP-equivalent registry` pattern):\n\n#### HPDC engineer (`HPDC_ENGINEER_REGISTRY_CID`)\n\n- Qualifications: Minimum 5 years industry HPDC experience (Buhler / Idra / Frech / Toshiba Machine class), OR equivalent academic credential (PhD metallurgy + thesis on die-casting solidification)\n- Responsibilities: Shot profile design + die thermal management + reject root-cause analysis\n- Council attestation: Lv6+ ≥3 with at least 1 Council member holding metallurgy / casting domain expertise\n\n#### Metallurgist (`METALLURGIST_REGISTRY_CID`)\n\n- Qualifications: Minimum 5 years industry experience in Al-Si alloy practice, OR equivalent academic credential (PhD metallurgy + thesis on Al-Si modification or HT-free alloy development)\n- Responsibilities: Alloy composition assay + Sr modification practice + companion test bar mechanical interpretation\n- Council attestation: Lv6+ ≥3\n\n#### 危険物取扱主任者-equivalent (`KIKENBUTSU_OPERATOR_REGISTRY_CID`)\n\n- Qualifications: Jurisdiction-licensed (JP: 甲種危険物取扱者 or equivalent; US: OSHA-certified high-pressure operator; EU: PED Module H or equivalent)\n- Responsibilities: Daily operations + emergency response + safety log per shift\n- Council attestation: Lv6+ ≥3 + safety-domain Council member endorsement\n- **Note**: G11 invariant says \"for >500 ton operations\". R1 = ≤500 ton (boundary). Registered as **precaution** since (a) day-to-day operator handling 700-750°C molten Al + 500 ton hydraulic intensification carries equivalent hazard regardless of force ceiling, and (b) R2 ramps to ≤2500 ton where G11 is unambiguously mandatory.\n\n### 4. Equipment Procurement Protocol — Second-Hand Revival Preferred\n\n**Critical §2(e) anti-gatekeeping clause**: religious-corp must not lock into IDRA / Buhler / Idra-Sayer new-build supply chain (vendor independence chain rationale per ADR-2605261200 §Rationale 4).\n\n**Acceptable equipment provenance** (in preference order):\n\n1. **Second-hand Buhler / Idra / Frech / Toshiba Machine** ≤500 ton class, ≥10 years post-original-purchase, with original firmware replaced by **open-source retrofit** (Linux-based real-time control + open WGS-84 PLC ladder logic + WASM state-machine for G8 replay determinism)\n2. **University surplus** from departments retiring research HPDC capacity (similar provenance + retrofit requirements)\n3. **New-build only IF** (a) clear-spec open-architecture vendor (no IDRA OL series; favor smaller Japanese makers like Toyo Machinery & Metal class with documented firmware API) AND (b) Council Lv6+ supermajority for purchase\n4. **Custom build from open-source HPDC machine reference design** — long-term ambition; documents publication of religious-corp HPDC reference design as §2(e)(i)(ii) anti-gatekeeping pro-clearance value (parallel to silicon Wave 1 iwakura/fuigo open RTL pattern)\n\n**Firmware retrofit requirements** (G3 + G8 invariants):\n\n- Shot profile @ 1 kHz logging mandatory; raw sensor stream + WASM state-machine seal CID published per shot\n- Vendor proprietary alloy recipes (e.g., Tesla AS3 closed composition) stripped on equipment intake — G2 + G6 invariants\n- Die-locking interlocks + ejector overload limits + thermal trip thresholds documented in open hardware description (HDL preferred; analog circuit schematics acceptable for legacy revival)\n\n### 5. Material Balance Relaxation — R1 ≥80% (R3 G10 ≥95%)\n\n**G10 R3 target = scrap recovery ≥95%**. R1 relaxation acknowledges:\n\n- First operator-led shots have higher reject rate (typical first-100-shot yield ~30-50%)\n- Sprue / runner geometry not yet optimized (multi-cavity = R2)\n- Die spray residue capture system not yet automated (Hibachi PoC = R2)\n- Crucible transfer losses higher with manual Otete handling (Tatara automated tending = R2)\n\n**R1 material balance invariant**: `recovered_mass / theoretical_loss ≥ 0.80` (vs. ≥0.95 R3). Recovery routes already in place:\n\n- Sprue + runner: shear-and-remelt next melt cycle (Otete handling)\n- Reject parts: full remelt (G10 invariant — never landfill)\n- Chip from `igata_trim_machining`: vacuum-extract to scrap bin\n- Flash: vibratory deburring → scrap bin\n- Die spray residue: manual collection R1 (R2 = Hibachi automated)\n\n**Path to ≥95% by R3**: Multi-cavity die (less sprue/runner loss), Hibachi (die-spray capture), Tatara (low-loss melt tending), improved first-pass yield.\n\n### 6. Cells Activated (7 of 8)\n\n**R1 activates** the following 7 cells (gate keys = `COUNCIL_CHARTER_ATTESTATION_TX_HASH` + `SILEN_IGATA_BASELINE_REVIEW_CID` + `HPDC_ENGINEER_REGISTRY_CID` + `METALLURGIST_REGISTRY_CID` + `KIKENBUTSU_OPERATOR_REGISTRY_CID` where applicable):\n\n| Cell | R1 PoC behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `igata_alloy_melt` | AlSi9Mg0.3 melt recipe; induction furnace ≤50 kg/batch; ICP-MS assay vs target; rotary degas + holding furnace transfer; emit `alloyAttestation` |\n| `igata_die_preparation` | H13 single-cavity die preheat 220°C; water-based release agent spray; 2D radiograph crack inspection (per-day); emit `dieReadyRecord` |\n| `igata_shot_injection` | ≤500 ton clamp verified; slow 0.15 m/s → fast 3.2 m/s → intensification 100 MPa × 2 s; @ 1 kHz logged; emit `castShotRecord` |\n| `igata_solidification_eject` | 5-sec dwell; clamp release + ejector advance; Otete pickup; HT-free natural air cool path (no quench R1); emit `ejectedPartRecord` |\n| `igata_post_cast_qc` | Mimi dimensional 3D scan vs CAD ±0.1 mm; 2D radiograph porosity screen (X-ray CT = R2); companion bar tensile per ASTM B557; surface visual; emit `qcAttestation` |\n| `igata_trim_machining` | Otete sprue/runner shear; vibratory deburring; CNC if datum-feature (LinuxCNC + FreeCAD Path); emit `trimmedPartRecord` |\n| `igata_part_attestation` | Lineage assembly + final visual + IPFS pin + material balance compute (R1 invariant ≥0.80); emit `partAttestation`; no cross-actor messages R1 (internal stock only) |\n\n**R1 cell wire (linear)**:\n```\nalloy_melt → die_preparation → shot_injection → solidification_eject →\n  post_cast_qc → trim_machining → part_attestation (skip heat_treatment R1)\n```\n\n**Skip path**: `trim_machining` emits `trimmedPartRecord` with `htRecipeUsed: \"HT-free\"` field; `part_attestation` accepts both `heatTreatedRecord` (R2+ path) and `trimmedPartRecord` (R1 path); R1 skip-HT branch is normal.\n\n### 7. `igata_heat_treatment` Stays R2-Gated\n\n**Reasoning** (G7 + G9 + G11 risk):\n\n- Solutionize furnace 500-540°C electric is high-energy point load (G9 budget squeeze)\n- Quench thermal shock + distortion risk (G14 documentation burden)\n- Hitogata class-A clean loading for high-T loading (R2+ class deferred)\n- T5 / T6 mechanical properties not required for ≤200 g R1 reference parts (HT-free yield ≥150 MPa sufficient)\n\n**R2 activation requires** (per future ADR-2605261230):\n- `R2_HT_RECIPE_BASELINE_CID` Council attestation (T5 + T6 protocol)\n- HT furnace equipment procurement (electric resistance ≤540°C ±2°C)\n- Quench bath (water 40-80°C; polymer optional for low-distortion class)\n- Distortion measurement protocol (Mimi 3D scan pre/post-HT)\n\n### 8. R1 Exit → R2 Entry Criteria\n\nR1 phase exits (and R2 ADR-2605261230 unlocks) when **all** of:\n\n1. **≥30 consecutive successful shots** (full @ 1 kHz log replayable, dimensional + porosity + mechanical all pass, no G11 incident)\n2. **Material balance ≥0.90** averaged over last 30 shots (path to R3 ≥0.95)\n3. **Multi-cavity die design Council-attested** (FreeCAD `.fcstd` + thermal simulation CID)\n4. **Vacuum-assist subsystem Council-attested** (design + safety review)\n5. **Hibachi PoC firmware tested** (open-source Rust, 3-axis high-T positioning + spray flow control, benchtop demo with mock die)\n6. **Tatara PoC firmware tested** (open-source Rust, induction furnace tending + rotary degasser remote control, benchtop demo with mock crucible)\n7. **30-day public comment window opened** (G13 invariant; parallel to yakushi Annex 1 facility audit pattern)\n8. **Annex-equivalent facility audit pass** — facility-level industrial hygiene + Charter Rider §2(g) supply chain review\n\n### 9. Constitutional Gates + Non-Goals Unchanged\n\n**No amendment** to ADR-2605261200 §Design `constitutionalGates` (G1..G14) or `nonGoals` (N1..N10). R1 invariants in §1 above are R-phase sub-ceilings / risk-graded relaxations within the IMMUTABLE constitutional envelope.\n\n**Explicit reconfirmation**:\n- G1 ≤6000 ton (R1 ≤500 ton sub-ceiling)\n- G2 Al-Si only (R1 baseline AlSi9Mg0.3)\n- G6 §2(a) military / aerospace structural NEVER (R1 reference parts = bracket / hinge / sensor housing = non-structural)\n- G7=NONE (R1 AlSi9Mg0.3 = 5-element + Sr modifier baseline; OPCW Schedule + RoHS + radioactive scan PASS)\n- G8 shot replay @ 1 kHz (R1 enforced from first shot)\n- G9 induction + electric only (R1 confirmed; energy meter logged)\n- G10 ≥95% recovery (R1 relaxed to ≥80%; R3 ramp path documented in §5)\n- G11 危険物取扱主任者 for >500 ton (R1 = boundary; SME registered as precaution)\n- G13 30-day notice + 1 km community feedback (enforced on facility procurement)\n- N1 giga press (≥7500 ton) — affirmed deferred post-R3 + Council Lv6+ supermajority\n- N2 + N3 military structural — affirmed NEVER (R1 reference parts geometry-cleared as non-military)\n- N8 mass-market consumer external — affirmed SBT↔SBT internal only (R1 = no external delivery)\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- **Operational HPDC readiness**: religious-corp first HPDC shot becomes possible after Council ratification — vendor independence chain first physical embodiment.\n- **§2(e) anti-gatekeeping concrete**: Second-hand revival + open-source firmware retrofit pattern documents religious-corp HPDC parameter library as world-first public reference. yakushi (off-patent OTC chemistry) + watatsumi (modular shipbuilding) + igata (HPDC parameters) form complementary anti-gatekeeping triplet.\n- **SME registration discipline**: 3-DID block (HPDC engineer + metallurgist + 危険物取扱主任者) mirrors yakushi QP-equivalent + 危険物取扱主任者 pattern. Council attestation discipline preserved.\n- **R2 path clear**: 8-criterion R1 exit gate is concrete and measurable; no ambiguity at R2 unlock.\n\n### Negative / Risk\n\n- **Equipment procurement timeline uncertain**: Second-hand ≤500 ton HPDC machines do not show up monthly. Realistic R1 activation window = 6-18 months after Council ratification (allow for international logistics via Funamori for non-domestic source). Material balance + safety practice during this lead time = paper review only.\n- **First-shot reject rate likely high**: 30-50% yield typical for first-100-shot HPDC operations even with experienced operators. Material balance R1 relaxation (≥80%) accounts for this; G10 R3 ≥95% remains the constitutional target.\n- **Hibachi + Tatara firmware = R2 dependency on R1 PoC bench**: The 2 new igata-native robotics classes (R2+ scope per ADR-2605261200) gain firmware PoC requirement in R1 exit criteria (§8 items 5-6). This is OK — R1 firmware can be tested with mock die / mock crucible without ramping HPDC clamp force.\n- **No cross-actor consumption R1**: `partAttestation` records emit internally; wadachi / tatekata / watatsumi / silicon Wave 2 consumers not yet wired. By design — R1 builds confidence; R2 + R3 ramp cross-actor.\n\n### Cross-actor integration (R-phase wire reference)\n\n| Consumer actor | igata supply | R-phase wire | R1 gate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| wadachi (autonomous mobility) | front/rear underbody, battery tray, motor housing | R3 only (G11 + N7) | R1 = NO |\n| tatekata (construction structural) | aluminum 柱頭 / 梁継手 / curtain-wall | R2 pilot OK | R1 = NO |\n| watatsumi (submersible) | ≤200 m class 補強材 ring section | R3 only | R1 = NO |\n| silicon Wave 2 | fab equipment frame structural | R2 bidirectional | R1 = NO |\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### A1: Skip R1, jump directly to R2 (≤2500 ton)\n\n- **Pros**: Faster path to industrial-class HPDC; bigger reference parts.\n- **Cons**: (1) ≤2500 ton equipment 100+ M JPY class — capital scale leap; (2) operator practice ramping should be graded; (3) Hibachi + Tatara PoC firmware needs R1 bench for testing without HPDC integration risk.\n- **Decision**: REJECT — R1 ≤500 ton bench-scale is the right capital + operator-learning gradient.\n\n### A2: Activate `heat_treatment` cell in R1\n\n- **Pros**: T6 mechanical properties (~250 MPa yield) more impressive than HT-free (~150 MPa).\n- **Cons**: (1) Solutionize furnace + quench bath = additional equipment scale + safety burden; (2) Hitogata class-A loading deferred R2+; (3) HT-free ≥150 MPa yield is sufficient for R1 reference parts (bracket / hinge / sensor housing all non-structural); (4) HT-free recipe is itself part of the religious-corp open-source contribution (parallel to Tesla AS3-equivalent open recipe).\n- **Decision**: REJECT — HT-free baseline first, T5 / T6 deferred to R2.\n\n### A3: Material balance R1 invariant = ≥0.95 (no relaxation)\n\n- **Pros**: G10 invariant honored from R1.\n- **Cons**: Unrealistic for first-100-shot operations. Operator-led ramp typically 30-50% first-pass yield. ≥95% recovery would require manual scrap retrieval discipline that contradicts G11 safety (handling 400-500°C ejected parts).\n- **Decision**: REJECT — R1 ≥0.80 with R3 ramp path documented in §5 is operationally honest.\n\n### A4: New-build ≤500 ton HPDC machine procurement\n\n- **Pros**: Latest firmware + warranty + support contract.\n- **Cons**: §2(e) anti-gatekeeping violation risk (vendor lock-in); capital scale 10x higher than second-hand; firmware retrofit required either way (G3 + G8); supports IDRA / Buhler / Idra-Sayer oligopoly.\n- **Decision**: REJECT (default); ALLOW only with Council Lv6+ supermajority + specific vendor selection vote (per §4 item 3).\n\n### A5: Defer SME registration to R2\n\n- **Pros**: Lighter Council load at R1.\n- **Cons**: (1) Operating any HPDC machine ≥100 ton without certified operator is a safety + insurance impossibility regardless of religious-corp framing; (2) yakushi Wave 1 set 危険物取扱主任者 + QP precedent for R1 even at lab-scale.\n- **Decision**: REJECT — SME registration is R1 hard gate per §3.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605261200 — igata R0 master charter (parent)\n- ADR-2605192100 — etzhayyim Mission Charter (§1.13 Wellbecoming, §1.12 Transparent Force)\n- ADR-2605192200 — Charter Compliance Rider v2.0 (§2(a) weapons, §2(e) anti-gatekeeping, §2(g) sustainability, §2(h) circular economy)\n- ADR-2605192300 — Bootstrap Council 5名 (Lv6+ ratification mechanism)\n- ADR-2605191524 — transparent force swarm broadcast witness quorum (G4 invariant)\n- ADR-2605201400 — kuni-umi planetary-infra fleet (Otete / Mimi / Hitogata robotics class lineage)\n- ADR-2605242545 — tsukuru fab 8-equipment Pregel charter (silicon EUV N1 deferral precedent)\n- ADR-2605242745 — silicon Wave 2 Funamori marine actor (raw ingot transport inheritance)\n- ADR-2605250500 — yakushi pharmaceutical master charter (Tier-B R0 14-gates + 10-non-goals canonical pattern)\n- ADR-2605250630 — yakushi Wave 1c R1 commissioning (R1 ADR structure precedent; chiral synthesis benchtop PoC + Council baseline + SME registration)\n- ADR-2605252200 — watatsumi civilian submersible R0 (YouTube methodology adoption + military exclusion pattern)\n- ADR-2605260200 — mitate R1 self-care advisory PWA (R1 cell activation precedent)\n- YouTube `y0oF2UirEMk` — IDRA Giga Press build-from-scratch documentary (methodology source, manufacturing methodology adopted, military / aerospace application rejected per §2(a))\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605261216-igata-r1-benchtop-commissioning.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "igata/megacasting/benchtop-hpdc", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-26T00:00:00Z", :adr/date "2026-05-26T00:00:00Z", :adr/authoritative true}]
